      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2119924570,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It might be good to add to the comment in `packet-e212.h` in front of the function that when `skip_first` is true, the high bit of the skipped nibble is treated as a odd/even indicator. I believe that is true in all the protocols that store the IMSI as a BCD skipping the first nibble (BSSAP and NAS for EPS do this)",
